{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And He saw</b>, the sixth day. Some say that \"the sixth\" is a construct form, meaning the sixth sphere, and likewise \"the seventh day.\" This is not so, and the phrase \"master of the sixth day\" according to the astrologers disproves it. Rather, its meaning is: the day that is sixth to the first day, and likewise \"the seventh day,\" as in \"the Israelite man\" (Leviticus 24:10), and many like it. Likewise רקיע השמים (Genesis 1:20): the raqi'a that is shamayim."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Resolved י\"א as יש אומרים ('some say') based on context; alternatively could read as י\"א = eleven, but that makes no sense here."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:43.465194804Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}